  "name": "Fur the 'More",
  "shortName": null,
  "description": "Fur the 'More (FtM) is an annual furry convention in the Baltimore-Washington area, organized by the Mid-Atlantic Anthropomorphic Association, Inc., a 501(c)(3). It began as an idea among Maryland furries who asked why Baltimore had no convention, and the first Fur the 'More was held April 5 to 7, 2013, at the Hunt Valley Inn near Baltimore, with the NorthEast Anthropomorphic Association as its backer. It moved to Tysons Corner, Virginia, in 2015, to the Hyatt Regency Crystal City in Arlington from 2020 to 2024, to the Hilton Washington Dulles Airport in Herndon in 2025, and to downtown Baltimore in 2026. The convention includes charity events, educational seminars, art shows and panels, and attendance has grown from 473 to nearly 1,900.",
